  "id": "2448c809-39fa-4fab-9b93-ac5bb5e88b7c",
  "title": "Central and Western Europe brace for more sweltering heat",
  "summary": "Central and western Europe is expected to experience more intense heatwaves as high pressure systems bring warm air from southern Europe, with forecasts showing temperatures reaching up to the high 30s celsius for France, Spain, Italy, and Germany. The heatwave has led to record-breaking temperatures in several European countries, including Slovakia and Austria, and has caused widespread evacuations and challenges in agriculture and water resources.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "France recorded over 5,700 excess deaths during its June heatwave, with southern Europe experiencing a record-breaking heatwave that has caused record crop losses and food price concerns.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Slovakia and Austria reached new high temperatures of 42C (108F) as authorities forced to shut down power plants due to extreme weather conditions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The heatwave in central and western Europe has led to record-breaking temperatures and widespread evacuations, with some countries facing significant climate-related challenges.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
